// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P540444702" "This piece could not possibly be part of a Clockwork construct."
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P3604073348" "Piece removed! Piece removed! Retrieve, retrieve!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3001004408" "You have defeated the Clockwork prince, Gearteeth. Unfortunately, no working Clockwork pieces could be salvaged. You did, however, discover something that Gearteeth was working on."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3693842938" "You didn't find a working piece, eh? That's too bad, but this unusual part you found more than makes up for it. I'd like to examine this; it isn't like anything I've seen the Clockwork King use before.<br><br>And he mentioned Faultline? Hrm...I wonder what he could be up to.<br><br>This combined with Dr. Vahzilok's plans worry me, {TaskForceName}. The city is faced with threats daily, but we may have some problems if two major villains are planning two plots at the same time.<br><br>I'll worry about that. For now, we have another problem to handle - the Circle of Thorns."
// RandomFameString :
"P2928093293" "Positron speaks highly of {TaskForceName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// RandomFameString :
"P863194669" "{TaskForceName} is the hottest thing around!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2205737870" "{HeroName}, with {TaskForceName}, correct? I'm glad you came. <br><br>I have the spell ready to send you into Oranbega. <br><br><color orange>Along with retrieving the book, you'll need to defeat the chief mages within and also destroy any obelisks you find. The obelisks...are key to the Circle empowering other magical spells that they have.</color><br><br>Are you ready?"
// Answer Text :
"P183133230" "Send me into Oranbega."
// Answer Text :
"P2901542335" "One moment."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2680879280" "Azuria contacted me regarding the Circle of Thorns. When I asked her why she contacted me, the <i>scientist</i> of the Phalanx, she said it was because, <color orange>'Numina told me that my path and the path of {TaskForceName} were destined to cross.'</color> So I hope you all don't mind looking into this, or else I'll never hear the end of it from Numina.<br><br>Anyway, some of the MAGI mystics have divined that the Circle are in possession of the <color yellow> Book of T'Jer'imikanu</color>.<br><br> According to Azuria, it's a very powerful spell book that contains <color yellow>Elder Magic</color>. From what Azuria has said, this is the same kind of magic wielded when the Mu first fought against the people of Oranbega thousands of years ago.<br><br> Their mystics within MAGI indicated that the Circle of Thorns have it somewhere inside their magical city of Oranbega.<br><br>Azuria informs me that she can use a spell to translocate a group of heroes into the section of Oranbega where the book is held, and then pull them out once they've gotten it. I told her that I had just the team of heroes for the job."
// AcceptString :
"P953657920" "Recover the Book."
// SendOffString :
"P3912522868" "Great, I knew I could count on you.<br><br>When you find the Book of T'Gerima... T'Geruni... the magic book, be really careful with it. It's the only known copy. According to MAGI It was thought to be destroyed in the Chicago fire of 1871.<br><br>Now get on over to MAGI and talk to Azuria, she'll get you where you need to go."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1123294516" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Elder Magic</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3851396000" "Teleport Assault into Oranbega"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4207407165" "I have no idea how to get into Oranbega. Azuria over at MAGI said she could teleport you to where the MAGI diviners located the Book of T'Geronimo... The Book."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3036077171" "Azuria's translocation magic leaves you disoriented for a moment, but when your senses clear you find yourself in the mythical city of Oranbega, home to the Circle of Thorns."
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P623572746" "Rollister says that the book will go far in summoning the Lance of Storms"
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION1 :
"P856629604" "What?! Intruders within the city?!"
// Script Variable INACTIVE_DIALOG_MINION2 :
"P1599791871" "Excellent. No one will be able to stop us now with the elder magic in hand!"
// Script Variable ATTACK_DIALOG_MINION2 :
"P2229687566" "Alert the others!"

