// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - PoisonTestSubject 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P1284192226" "Test subject"
// Description :
"P701875376" "Find a blood sample"
// InteractBeginString :
"P648584803" "You begin to extract a blood sample."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2852363772" "You have extracted a blood sample."
// InteractActionString :
"P2335543567" "Extracting..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2403097735" "You have stopped the Vahzilok operation and recovered some evidence."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P949825334" "Good job in bringing in Doc Buzzsaw!<br><br>Phase three...and the Faultline project? This doesn't bode well, {TaskForceName}.<br><br>At any rate, this blood sample is a great step forward. Hopefully I can work out a counter-agent to the Vahzilok poison before they get to phase three.<br><br>Wait, what was that about Excelsior?<br><br>Of course! Now it all makes sense! That 2% of the formula! I knew I'd seen it somewhere before. It's Excelsior! Or rather, small traces of it.<br><br>The Vahzilok must be experimenting with mixing their chemical compound with Excelsior in order to increase the success rate of grafting different tissues together. Or worse yet, grafting cybernetics to their walking corpses.<br><br>I'll have to study this blood sample and see how it has reacted with the victim's blood. Only then will I be able to figure out what the Vahzilok are aiming to do. This can't be good though if it has to do with Faultline as well.<br><br>We should see about that Clockwork lead of -<br><br><color orange>Positron's communicator goes off with an SOS signal.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MsLibertyDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P77716562" "I'm guessing you know why Atlas Park suddenly came under attack by the Circle of Thorns. <i>All</i> the Circle of Thorns!"
// Answer Text :
"P3973768321" "Mention the Book of T'Jer'imikanu."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P529788380" "I see...okay, we're still fine, for now, {TaskForceName}.<br><br>They haven't managed to breach city hall just yet.<br><br>Most of the heroes managed to spread out through the city, but some of them are pinned down here by the Circle!"
// Answer Text :
"P443546093" "We'll rescue the heroes here, you organize the others in the city!"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P4127830658" "Good idea! I'll get on it. <br><br><color orange>Tell the heroes you rescue here to meet me in the southern end of Atlas!"
// Answer Text :
"P1035546980" "Sounds good, Ms. Liberty, let's do this!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - AzuriaDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P65794489" "Tarses and the Circle took the book!"
// Answer Text :
"P2264105771" "Ask how the Circle got into City Hall."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P4204907893" "They arrived without warning. They must have traced my translocation spell back here and used it to open a gate straight through the magical wardings."
// Answer Text :
"P1326004239" "Ask if Azuria is alright."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P2417503663" "I... I'm fine. If you hadn't arrived when you did, though, I might not have been.<br><br>Thank you {TaskForceName}, I owe you my life."
// Answer Text :
"P602285070" "Ask Azuria what she discovered in the book."
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P1039844200" "Yes, of course.<br><br>Before the Circle arrived and stole the book back I had found several passages of interest, specifically pertaining to this Lance of Storms ritual as well as a method for creating Shadow Simulacrums."
// Answer Text :
"P2729280918" "Ask about the Lance of Storms."
// Answer Text :
"P4232147116" "Ask about the Shadow Simulacrums."
// Page LanceOfStorms1 Text :
"P2780019389" "According to the book, there is a ritual that draws upon the power of storms, manifesting it into a potent weapon which can be directed against one's enemies.<br><br>I collaborated with Numina and she spoke with agents of Ignis, the Entity of Weather, and they confirm that no storms are headed to Paragon City any time soon. So at least that gives us time to track the book down again."
// Page ShadowSimulacrums1 Text :
"P1238337919" "It is obvious to me now that Rollister, the Circle Mage that was leading the attack, has mastered the art of creating Shadow Simulacrums.<br><br>Who knows what devastation the Circle plans to unleash with the ability to make shadowy duplicates of Paragons greatest heroes."
// Answer Text :
"P3281878713" "Thank Azuria for the information and leave."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1959942352" "{TaskForceName}, we've got a serious problem! <br><br>I was just contacted by <color yellow>Ms. Liberty</color>. Somehow the Circle of Thorns have attacked the very heart of Atlas Park and are now on a mad rampage throughout the city! <br><br>She doesn't know how it happened but she needs help, fast!<br><br>I need you all to get down to Atlas Park and get the situation under control with Ms. Liberty! In the meantime I'm going to head to Faultline to make sure this isn't some sort of distraction by the Circle!"
// AcceptString :
"P3531622857" "Save Atlas Park!"
// SendOffString :
"P4256602317" "Take the trolley, {TaskForceName}, it'll get you straight there! Once you arrive, seek out Ms. Liberty at once.<br><br>If I need your backup at the dam, I'll be sure to send you a message."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3540407781" "<color deepskyblue>Part Five: Reflection</color>"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1768487526" "There's no time to waste, {TaskForceName}!"

